{"comparisons":[],"failures":[],"frontier":[],"initial":{"normative":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Establishes the extended parallel run and compulsory route from 30 November 2024.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u1"},{"reason":"Background heading; no independent duty.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u2"},{"reason":"Identifies the launch, WINGS platform, submission types and earlier circular; the earlier circular is not supplied.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u3"},{"reason":"Explains parallel running as continued acceptance of existing submission channels.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u4"},{"reason":"Heading for extension and enhancements.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u5"},{"reason":"Reports monitoring and industry engagement; imposes no submission duty.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u6"},{"reason":"Confirms extension to 29 November 2024; planned enhancements explain the extension.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u7"},{"reason":"Heading supporting the full-adoption context.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u8"},{"reason":"Restates the mandatory route, identifies integrated reporting and separately permits annual-fee payment.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u9"},{"reason":"Enquiries heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u10"},{"reason":"Operational review statement and contact invitation; the practicability qualification concerns SFC enhancements.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u11"},{"reason":"Identifies the issuing division.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u12"},{"reason":"Identifies the issuing regulator.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u13"},{"reason":"Closing marker.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u14"},{"reason":"Identifies product categories associated with the IPD scope; exhaustiveness is unresolved.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u17"},{"reason":"Expands WINGS without adding a separate route requirement.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u18"}],"dimensions":[{"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The requirement attaches to applications and submissions concerning investment products administered by IPD. It applies to persons making those submissions, without identifying a particular regulated actor class or creating a general duty to submit.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u9","u17"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"e-IP is the investment-product application/submission system on WINGS, whose expansion is supplied. Footnote 1 lists product categories but does not expressly state whether the list exhaustively defines IPD-administered products.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u17","u18"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"Existing channels remain available during the extended parallel run. No post-transition exception is stated. The phrase 'where practicable' qualifies SFC review and enhancement, not the compulsory submission route.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u4","u7","u9","u11"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"'Must' establishes the compulsory route. Integration and enhancements are announced system changes. 'Can also' describes an optional annual-fee payment facility; the enquiry invitation adds no mandatory filing step.","source_unit_ids":["u7","u9","u11"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The 29 July 2024 launch and original 29 October 2024 parallel-run endpoint are historical context. The extension carries parallel running through 29 November 2024, with compulsory e-IP use beginning on 30 November 2024. No express grandfathering rule for pending matters is supplied.","source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u4","u7","u9"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The 8 July 2024 circular and external-authorities.24ec50 dependency are not supplied. Their possible definitions, procedural conditions or exceptions cannot be resolved. Integration of existing IP E-submission requests does not itself establish the underlying reporting triggers or deadlines.","source_unit_ids":["u3","u9"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["Does footnote 1 exhaustively define the covered products, or identify categories within the broader class of products administered by IPD?","Does the 8 July 2024 circular or the unavailable external dependency specify exceptions, outage arrangements or treatment of submissions in matters initiated before 30 November 2024?","Which existing IP E-submission requests qualify as covered submissions, and what separate sources establish their reporting triggers and deadlines?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["Extending the parallel run extends its stated feature of accepting existing channels through 29 November 2024.","The transition applies by the date of each submission event; the supplied text provides no exemption based on when the underlying matter began.","Whether a particular product and communication fall within the IPD submission scope must be established separately; unknown classifications remain unknown."],"citations":[{"quote":"After the extended period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by the Investment Products Division (IPD)1 must be submitted to IPD via e-IP from 30 November 2024.","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.","unit_id":"u4"},{"quote":"To facilitate these enhancements, the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.","unit_id":"u7"},{"quote":"Starting 30 November 2024, ie, after the parallel run period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by IPD must be submitted via e-IP.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.","unit_id":"u9"},{"quote":"The SFC will continue to review and enhance the operation of e-IP where practicable.","unit_id":"u11"},{"quote":"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.","unit_id":"u17"}],"distinction":"This reading tests the route used for an individual covered submission from the transition date. It neither makes annual-fee payment through e-IP compulsory nor creates underlying reporting obligations. The strongest uncertainty is the precise product and communication scope, including any qualifications in the unavailable earlier circular. The supplied text does not support a materially different transition date or a general post-transition choice of channels.","family":"time","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The evaluated event is an application or submission to IPD concerning an investment product administered by IPD. Classification must account for footnote 1; optional fee payment alone does not establish this fact.","name":"is_covered_submission","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u3","u9","u17"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean classification of one submission event"},{"meaning":"Gregorian calendar date on which the evaluated application or submission is made to IPD.","name":"submission_date","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"The evaluated application or submission is submitted to IPD via e-IP.","name":"submitted_via_eip","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u9"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean route observation for one submission event"}],"result":"submitted_via_eip","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_covered_submission (>= submission_date (date 2024-11-30)))"},"local_id":"r1","questions":["Do any omitted provisions qualify the submission-date treatment of pending matters?","Is footnote 1 exhaustive, and how are borderline communications classified?"],"statement":"Selected control: compulsory e-IP submission route after the extended parallel run. Existing channels remain available through 29 November 2024. For each covered application or submission made from 30 November 2024, the submitter must use e-IP. Existing reporting requests are announced as integrated into e-IP, while annual-fee payment through the system remains optional. The practicability qualification concerns SFC enhancements only.","subject":"Route used for an individual application or submission concerning an IPD-administered investment product"}]}},"java_checks":[],"live_provider":true,"model_calls":2,"no_progress":0,"nodes":[],"pending":null,"provider_id":"codex.fresh.v1","retrievals":[],"rounds":0,"roundtrips":[],"run_id":"run.d5b61eecc495480180a4d6d5f05af074","stop":null}